WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:06.240
Ever since I could remember I liked
making stuff. I'd just make things. You

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:09.570
know? My backgrounds really pottery is
really ceramics, touching the clay,

00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:15.470
touching the mud, making things with
clay - so the clay is mixed with about 50%

00:00:15.470 --> 00:00:20.340
sawdust - dry clay, dry sawdust - but more
and more as I started to do that

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:26.039
I also had this little, I don't know what
it was, this urge, ability, interest for

00:00:26.039 --> 00:00:30.330
teaching for education. Making stuff and
teaching stuff well actually you can do

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:33.540
that, that's called the being an art
educator or a teacher. The idea was that

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:37.309
the making, and the teaching, and the
learning, and the asking of questions -

00:00:37.309 --> 00:00:41.940
through art, through the visual imagery
that you're talking about - that was what

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:45.719
was so important. To search for the good
and make it matter this is the real

00:00:45.719 --> 00:00:51.050
challenge of the artist. The kind of
group that has self-assembled today

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:57.690
speaks to multiple interests that I have.
Henry felt like singing, but slaves

00:00:57.690 --> 00:01:03.750
didn't dare sing in the streets, instead
he hummed all the way home. And trying to

00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:07.710
weave it into what is an art education
how does one learn through the making of

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:13.530
things through cultural production - this 
filter has been filtering water - what kind

00:01:13.530 --> 00:01:18.600
of questions can we ask? Not just about
what someone else has made, but what kind

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:22.320
of questions can we ask through the act
of making itself? I'm thrilled that

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:25.860
you're all here you're thinking about
these ideas I hope you take back even a

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:29.400
small bit of what we've talked about
what you've heard from others into your

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:35.659
own teaching experiences and perhaps in
some way our conversation can continue.

00:01:40.110 --> 00:01:42.170
 

